    fields:  # 57c9
      severity: "low"  # 57c9
      statement: "Five field names appear in both edge.meta (22 distinct keys) and node.meta (42 distinct keys): query_type, queue_type, topic, topic_type, url_path. The value distributions differ between contexts: url_path on edges is {/ws: 12}; url_path on nodes is {/api/users: 10, /api/users/1: 1, /api: 1} — entirely disjoint value sets. queue_type on edges peaks at 'kafka' (85); on nodes peaks at 'kafka' (55) but with redis (9) appearing at node-scope only. The same field-name carries the same semantic concept but different mechanical scopes: edge-meta describes the edge relationship; node-meta describes the node. Schema does not document the dual-scope semantics; consumers may merge or split them inconsistently."  # 57c9
      root_cause: "Two independent emitters (linker-side edge.meta vs analyzer-side node.meta) coined the same field name for related-but-distinct semantics. The schema treats edge.meta and node.meta as namespace-separate so the collision doesn't cause runtime issues but introduces conceptual confusion. Same family as pass-19 GGGGGGG (construct vs call_construct) but at the cross-scope level rather than within-scope."  # 57c9
